      "content": "Even a small amount of alcohol can interact dangerously with Ambien, even if you don't feel intoxicated. Alcohol enhances the sedative effects of zolpidem, making your drowsiness much more pronounced. Because of this increased risk of central nervous system depression, it's best to avoid combining them altogether for a safer night's sleep. Always err on the side of caution when mixing medications and alcohol.",
      "source": "target",
