      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the timing gives your body some time to process the alcohol, the sedative effects can linger and still interact with your medication. Both substances affect the central nervous system, and their effects can compound each other regardless of the small time gap. For the safest and most predictable sleep, it is strongly advised to separate the wine completely from the time you take Ambien. Your doctor is the best resource to give you specific guidance based on your health.",
      "source": "target",
